'''''Phalaris aquatica''''' (also known as '''''P. tuberosa''''', '''Bulbous canary-grass''' or '''Harding grass''') is a plant in the [[:category:Phalaris (genus)|Phalaris genus]]. It contains approximately 0.100% [[DMT]]<ref name=smith>{{cite journal | vauthors=((Smith, T. A.)) | journal=Phytochemistry | title=Tryptamine and related compounds in plants | volume=16 | issue=2 | pages=171–175 | date= 1977 | url=https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0031942200867783 | issn=00319422 | doi=10.1016/S0031-9422(00)86778-3}}</ref><ref name=erowid>{{Citation | title=Erowid Phalaris Vault : FAQ 2.01 | url=https://www.erowid.org/plants/phalaris/phalaris_faq.shtml}}</ref>, 0.022% [[5-MeO-DMT]]<ref name=smith></ref><ref name=erowid></ref>, and 0.005% [[bufotenin]].<ref name=erowid></ref>

